From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:45:06 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 104/144] GreatDANE: privacy wording: "The server logs",
 Analytics sentence, GMP %DISTRIBUTION% (NGD round 4, L-i)

- PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md and the PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy comment: "The servers log" becomes "The server logs",
  matching the single update server (pepecoin.surf).
- The "Analytics is not claimed for it ... (NGD final manifest ruling)" sentence is replaced. It wrongly
  attributed this to NGD, who ruled that Analytics stays. Both files now read: "For the Dane update check the
  purpose is AppFunctionality only; the entry also carries Analytics because of Mozilla's opt-in telemetry."
- L-i: the GMP URL list now has the full media.gmp-manager.url path from all.js:3474:
  .../%OS_VERSION%/%DISTRIBUTION%/%DISTRIBUTION_VERSION%/update.xml. The sent fields now include
  distribution ID and version.
- Plist values are unchanged.
---
 greatdane/macos/PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md   | 8 ++++----
 greatdane/macos/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy | 8 +++++---
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/greatdane/macos/PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md b/greatdane/macos/PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md
index f5ab9b1745..1db0171554 100644
--- a/greatdane/macos/PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md
+++ b/greatdane/macos/PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md
@@ -20,10 +20,10 @@ If a feature only collects after the user turns it on, it's still declared.
 
 **What Dane's own servers see.** This corrects the earlier "Dane's own servers receive nothing".
 - **Update check** (`app.update.url`, browser/app/profile/firefox.js:3719). It's declared under the existing
-  OtherDiagnosticData entry: Linked=false, Tracking=false, purpose AppFunctionality. Analytics is not claimed for it,
-  because nothing shows the logs are used to count installs (NGD final manifest ruling, 2026-11-10).
+  OtherDiagnosticData entry: Linked=false, Tracking=false, purpose AppFunctionality.
+  For the Dane update check the purpose is AppFunctionality only; the entry also carries Analytics because of Mozilla's opt-in telemetry.
 
-  The automatic update check sends product, version, build ID, target, locale and channel to Dane's update server (pepecoin.surf). The servers log only product, version, platform and channel, plus the request status, the user agent and a masked IP (/24 for IPv4, /48 for IPv6). Build ID, locale, query strings and referrers are not logged. Logs are kept about 14 days, are not linked to an account or device, and are not shared. Entries from before Nov 10, 2026 hold full IPs until they rotate out around Nov 25. No check happens while the DisableAppUpdate policy is on.
+  The automatic update check sends product, version, build ID, target, locale and channel to Dane's update server (pepecoin.surf). The server logs only product, version, platform and channel, plus the request status, the user agent and a masked IP (/24 for IPv4, /48 for IPv6). Build ID, locale, query strings and referrers are not logged. Logs are kept about 14 days, are not linked to an account or device, and are not shared. Entries from before Nov 10, 2026 hold full IPs until they rotate out around Nov 25. No check happens while the DisableAppUpdate policy is on.
 
   Plainly: log entries written before Nov 10, 2026 kept full client IPs, and they stay on the server until they
   rotate out around Nov 25, 2026. The update URL is https://pepecoin.surf/dane/update/3/... (dogecoin.surf only
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@ If a feature only collects after the user turns it on, it's still declared.
